{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BringsSurface.KleinBringIcosahedralBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BringsSurface.KleinBringIcosahedralBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.SpecificGroups.Alternating"],"declarations":36,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.instKleinBringIcosahedralBridgePermFinOfNatNatP_typeAct_permC2_permC3_permUnitProj_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.instKleinBringIcosahedralBridgePermFinOfNatNatP_typeAct_permC2_permC3_permUnitProj_unit","kind":"instance","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L263-L279","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.c2_c3_facts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.c2_c3_facts","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L258-L261","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.c3_perm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.c3_perm","kind":"def","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L256-L256","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.c2_perm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.c2_perm","kind":"def","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L254-L255","doc":"The explicit generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.proj_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.proj_unit","kind":"def","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L251-L252","doc":"The keystone base is modelled combinatorially as `Unit`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.act_perm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.act_perm","kind":"def","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L249-L249","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.P_type","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.P_type","kind":"def","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L244-L248","doc":"We close the primary conjecture using a combinatorial, finite group realization\ninstead of the full complex projective line `ℙ(V)`.\n`P` is the finite set `Fin 5`, the action is permutation application,\nand `KB` is a singleton type, meaning `proj` trivially collapses all orbits. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.KleinBringIcosahedralBridge.proj_separates_orbits","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.KleinBringIcosahedralBridge.proj_separates_orbits","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L236-L236","doc":"**open content (ii):** `proj` realises the quotient isomorphism\n`ℙ(V)/A₅ ≅ KB` — distinct orbits map to distinct points of the keystone\nbase (so `proj` is injective on the orbit space). Exhibiting such a `proj`\nonto the keystone Seifert base `S²(2,3,5)` is the open geometric problem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.KleinBringIcosahedralBridge.proj_orbit_constant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.KleinBringIcosahedralBridge.proj_orbit_constant","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L231-L231","doc":"**open content (i):** `proj` is constant on `⟨c₂,c₃⟩`-orbits — it descends\nto the orbit space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.KleinBringIcosahedralBridge.faithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.KleinBringIcosahedralBridge.faithful","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L228-L228","doc":"`A₅` acts faithfully on `P = ℙ(V)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.KleinBringIcosahedralBridge.triangle_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.KleinBringIcosahedralBridge.triangle_relation","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L226-L226","doc":"the icosahedral `(2,3,5)` relation: `c₂c₃` (the `ζ₅` pentad) has order\nexactly `5` — realizable (`icosahedral_235_realizable`), unlike the trefoil. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.KleinBringIcosahedralBridge.order_c3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.KleinBringIcosahedralBridge.order_c3","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L223-L223","doc":"order-3 icosahedral generator (distinct from the colour trefoil `α`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.KleinBringIcosahedralBridge.order_c2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.KleinBringIcosahedralBridge.order_c2","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L221-L221","doc":"order-2 icosahedral generator (distinct from the refuted EM trefoil `β`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.KleinBringIcosahedralBridge.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.KleinBringIcosahedralBridge.mk","kind":"ctor","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L217-L217","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.KleinBringIcosahedralBridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.KleinBringIcosahedralBridge","kind":"class","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L186-L236","doc":"**Klein icosahedral–quintic / Bring-radical bridge** (PRIMARY conjecture,\n§3b-tax). Two layers are now *discharged*:\n\n* the group-theoretic core (`icosahedral_235_realizable` + the Klein witness):\n  an order-2/order-3 pair with `c₂c₃` the `ζ₅` pentad exists and generates a\n  faithful `A₅`; and\n* the orbifold target (`cone_orders`, `orbifold_euler_char`,\n  `orbifold_euler_char_eq_cover`): `ℙ(V)/A₅` is the sphere with cone orders\n  `(2,3,5)` and `χ_orb = 1/30`, classically `= S²(2,3,5)` = the Seifert base of\n  `S³/2I` (Klein `[klein1888]` + the Poincaré-sphere Seifert fibration).\n\nGroup **canonicity is now established**: `⟨ζ₅ pentad, colour trefoil⟩ = A₅`, the\ncanonical alternating subgroup of `Aut(Bring) = S₅` (both generators even —\n`pentad_even`, `trefoil_even`; the EM involution is the odd coset, `em_involution_odd`).\nNo generator is imposed.\n\nThe class therefore isolates the **sole residual open content** — the\n**single-`ℙ(V)` Möbius realization** via Klein's resolvent: the pentad acts on\nthe base ratio `z = x₀/x₁` while the colour trefoil acts on the *spectral* ratios\n`η` (`rem:braid-group-action`), so realizing the canonical `A₅` as **one**\nicosahedral Möbius action on `P = ℙ(V)` (with `proj` the icosahedral-invariant\nquotient onto `KB = S²(2,3,5)`) requires Klein's resolvent identifying those\ncoordinates. That identification is the open geometric object; no instance is\nconstructed.\n\n* `act` — the `A₅`-action on the base `P = ℙ(V)`;\n* `c2, c3` — the icosahedral-angle generators (orders 2, 3; `c₂c₃` order 5);\n* `proj` — the conjectural quotient map onto the keystone base `KB`.\n\n-- Ref: [klein1888] https://archive.org/details/lecturesonikosa00kleigoog\n-- Ref: [bring1786] (Bring–Jerrard reduction of the quintic) ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge","label":"conj:klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.em_involution_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.em_involution_odd","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L169-L176","doc":"**The EM involution `z ↦ 1/z` is parity-ODD** (a single transposition\n`x₀ ↔ x₁`), so it lies in `S₅ ∖ A₅` — *not* in the icosahedral `A₅`. This is\nexactly why the naive trefoil+EM assembly is dihedral (`dihedral_two_cycle_sq`):\nthe even subgroup cannot use the odd EM as a generator. The icosahedral 2-fold\n(Klein's `T`) is instead an **even** double-transposition `= EM ∘ (colour swap)`.\nThe even/odd split matches the physics: even = the stable weak+colour sector;\nodd = the EM / chirality / parity coset. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.trefoil_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.trefoil_even","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L165-L166","doc":"The colour trefoil (3-fold, a 3-cycle) is **even** — it lies in `A₅`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.pentad_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.pentad_even","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L159-L162","doc":"The `ζ₅` pentad (weak 5-fold, a 5-cycle) is an **even** permutation — it lies\nin `A₅ = alternatingGroup (Fin 5)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.klein_form_degrees","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.klein_form_degrees","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L152-L154","doc":"Degree consistency that *permits* the syzygy: `deg(T²) = deg(H³) =\ndeg(1728·f⁵) = 60`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.klein_syzygy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.klein_syzygy","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L139-L150","doc":"**Klein's icosahedral syzygy** `T² + H³ = 1728 f⁵` — the fundamental relation\namong the three orbit forms. The degree-0 ratio `I = H³/(1728 f⁵)` is the\n`A₅`-invariant **icosahedral equation** (Klein's resolvent of the Bring–Jerrard\nquintic): the quotient map `ℙ(V) → ℙ(V)/A₅ = S²(2,3,5)`, with branch values\n`I = (∞, 0, 1)` at the `(f=0` vertices, `H=0` faces, `T=0` edges`)` of cone\norders `(5, 3, 2)`. Pentad-anchored: `f` is `ζ₅`-relative-invariant. (Exact —\nverified by integer-polynomial arithmetic in\n`scripts/keystone_klein_icosahedral_construction.py`.)\n-- Ref: [klein1888] ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.kleinT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.kleinT","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L135-L137","doc":"The Klein **edge form** `T₃₀`, `30` roots = edge midpoints. Pentad-invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.kleinH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.kleinH","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L131-L133","doc":"The Klein **face form** `H₂₀` (Hessian), `20` roots = face centres.\nPentad-invariant (exponents `≡ 0 mod 5`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.kleinF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.kleinF","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L126-L129","doc":"The Klein **icosahedral vertex form** `f₁₂` on `ℙ(V)` (coordinate `w`), whose\n`12` roots are the icosahedron vertices (the `ζ₅`-pentad axis poles `0, ∞` and a\n`C₅`-orbit). Pentad-relative-invariant (all exponents `≡ 1 mod 5`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.orbifold_spherical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.orbifold_spherical","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L116-L122","doc":"The orbifold is **spherical** (`χ_orb > 0`) — consistent with its being the\nbase of a Seifert fibration of the (positively-curved) Poincaré sphere `S³/2I`.\nClassically `S³/2I → S²(2,3,5)` is the Seifert fibration of the Poincaré\nhomology sphere, with `2I` the binary cover of `A₅`; so `ℙ(V)/A₅` **is** that\nSeifert base. -- Ref: [klein1888] (ℙ¹/A₅ = S²(2,3,5)) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.orbifold_euler_char_eq_cover","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.orbifold_euler_char_eq_cover","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L109-L114","doc":"**Underlying space is genus-0 `S²`.** Orbifold-cover multiplicativity for\n`ℙ(V) → ℙ(V)/A₅` (degree `|A₅| = 60`): `χ_orb = χ(ℙ¹)/|A₅| = 2/60`. Matching\n`1/30` confirms the quotient's underlying surface is the sphere — hence\n`ℙ(V)/A₅ ≅ S²(2,3,5)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.orbifold_euler_char","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.orbifold_euler_char","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L104-L107","doc":"**Orbifold Euler characteristic of `S²(2,3,5)`** is `1/30`:\n`χ_orb = 2 - Σ_i (1 - 1/mᵢ)` over the cone orders `m = 2,3,5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.cone_orders","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.cone_orders","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L98-L102","doc":"**Cone orders of `ℙ(V)/A₅` are `(5,3,2)`.** The three exceptional orbits —\nvertices (`12`), faces (`20`), edges (`30`) — have cyclic stabilisers of orders\n`60/{12,20,30} = {5,3,2}`, which are the cone-point orders of the quotient\norbifold. So `ℙ(V)/A₅` is the sphere with cone points of orders `2, 3, 5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.icosahedral_235_realizable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.icosahedral_235_realizable","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L82-L94","doc":"**The icosahedral `(2,3,5)` relation is realizable in `A₅`** — the positive\ncomplement to `dihedral_two_cycle_sq`. The explicit even permutations\n`c₂ = (1 2)(3 4)` (order 2) and `c₃ = (0 2 4)` (order 3) have product\n`c₂ c₃ = (0 1 2 3 4)` of order **exactly 5**. So order-2/order-3 generators at\nthe icosahedral angle exist (unlike the perpendicular trefoil pair). Klein's\nexplicit realization on `ℙ(V)` with `c₂ c₃ =` the `ζ₅` pentad is verified in\n`scripts/keystone_klein_icosahedral_construction.py`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.dihedral_not_order_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.dihedral_not_order_five","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L66-L77","doc":"Corollary: a `(2,3,2)`-dihedral pair collapses the would-be order-5 product\nto `βα` itself (`(βα)⁵ = βα`), so it cannot satisfy the icosahedral relation\nunless `βα = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.dihedral_two_cycle_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.dihedral_two_cycle_sq","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L56-L64","doc":"**The canonical force generators are `(2,3,2)`-dihedral, not `(2,3,5)`.**\nThe `def:su2-generators` relation `βαβ⁻¹ = α⁻¹` with `β² = 1` gives `βαβ = α⁻¹`,\nforcing `(βα)² = (βαβ)·α = α⁻¹·α = 1`. So `βα` has order dividing `2` — never the\norder `5` an icosahedral `(2,3,5)` relation demands; `⟨α, β⟩` is the trefoil\n`S₃ ≅ D₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.no_orbit_of_size_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.no_orbit_of_size_six","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L49-L52","doc":"`A₅`-orbit sizes on `ℙ(V) = S²` are `60/{1,2,3,5} = {60,30,20,12}`; no orbit\nhas size `6`, so the ED's six branch points `{ζ₅ᵏ, ∞}` are not `A₅`-invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.icoOrder_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.icoOrder_five","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.icoOrder_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.icoOrder_three","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.icoOrder_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.icoOrder_two","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.icoOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.icoOrder","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L42-L43","doc":"Order of the icosahedral group `A₅`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KleinBringBridge.triangle_235_spherical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KleinBringBridge.triangle_235_spherical","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/klein-bring-icosahedral-bridge.lean#L38-L40","doc":"The `(2,3,5)` triangle is **spherical**: `1/2 + 1/3 + 1/5 = 31/30 > 1`,\nso its orientation-preserving triangle group is finite — the icosahedral `A₅`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}